                <pb facs="0520" n="516" sameAs="frus:frus1938v03/pg516"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/13975: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-09-29T09:00:00+07:00">September 29, 1938—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 29—8 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>570. My 469, September 28, 1 p.m.<anchor n="66" xml:id="d524-f1"/> In my
                    interview with the Minister for Foreign Affairs yesterday he informed me that he
                    had received word that League had voted to apply sanctions against Japan and he
                    again expressed the hope that United States would support the League in any way
                    within its power.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
